data.content:
**Yes, C# fully supports `stackalloc` into a `Span<nint>` and `Span<nuint>`.** Both compiled and ran without issue:

```csharp
Span<nint>  signed   = stackalloc nint[4];
Span<nuint> unsigned = stackalloc nuint[3];
```

On this 64-bit system `nint.Size` is 8 bytes, so each element is pointer-sized. This has been supported since C# 9 / .NET 5 (when `nint`/`nuint` were introduced as first-class types backed by `System.IntPtr`/`System.UIntPtr`).
